Z||000000||V8Fiero||10-01-2000||06:00 PM||||Hello guys,<P> I know that I have seen a thread on this before but couldnt find it. I am purchasing another fiero in a couple of weeks. It has been sitting for about 2 yrs. The guy said that it ran before it was parked. <P>What all is needed to try and start this bad boy up to see if she runs? Maybe wont part it out, just sell it as a whole.<P>TIA<BR>Scooter||||reg||5
Z||000001||Fearless Freep||10-01-2000||06:11 PM||||Hmmm...battery....also I had read somewhere here about putting a drop of oil down each spark plug hole?  Anyone help me out with this one??||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-01-2000||06:12 PM||||Keys are always a good starting point. j/k||||reg||1
Z||000003||Seanh||10-01-2000||06:14 PM||||Yeah, you can put some oil down the spark plug holes. It will help lube the head since the oil is probally going to take some time to get moving trougt the engine.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000004||V8Fiero||10-01-2000||06:46 PM||||10,000 comedians out of work and I think half of them own fieros. j/k LOL.<P>Yea that kind of what I was looking for. Priming the cylinders with oil. It has the four speed manual. Anything special to do with that?<P>||||reg||10
Z||000005||ThatRickGuy||10-02-2000||08:55 AM||||Some of that Gas cleaner and some fresh gas would also help. Pump gas gets pretty nasty after sitting for a few months and can really screw with the injectors.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wade87GT||10-02-2000||11:34 AM||||After you put some oil in the plug holes, try cranking it over without the sparkplugs installed (remove the coil wire also). This can help lube the cylinder walls and the piston rings without fighting against the forces of compression.||||reg||1
